"""Class 9 NEW Writing+Grammar sets 1-5 (30 marks): W = notice(4) OR, formal letter/email(5) OR, speech/article(5) OR, narrative essay(6) OR; G = paragraph completion (4) + rearrangement (3) + transformation (3)."""
from eng9_lib import Q, OR, P, S
def m(q, o): return S(q, "a", 1, o)
def N(q, ans): return Q(q, ans, "4")
def L(q, ans): return Q(q, ans, "5")
def A(q, ans): return Q(q, ans, "5")
def E(q, ans): return Q(q, ans, "6")
def g(q, ans): return Q(q, ans, "1")
FL = "<br><i>(Format 1 · Content 2 · Organisation 1 · Language 1)</i>"
FA = "<br><i>(Content 2 · Organisation 1 · Expression/Style 1 · Accuracy 1)</i>"
FE = "<br><i>(Content 2 · Organisation 1 · Expression 2 · Accuracy 1)</i>"
SETS = {}

SETS[1] = dict(W=[
 OR(N("Your school is organising a Book Fair. Write a notice in not more than 50 words giving details. You are the Head Boy/Head Girl.", "<b>NOTICE</b><br>Mastermind Public School, Jaipur<br>2 November 2026<br><b>BOOK FAIR</b><br>A Book Fair will be held in the school hall from 9 to 11 November 2026, 9 a.m. to 3 p.m. Books on fiction, science and general knowledge will be available at 10% discount. Students may visit during recess and after school.<br>Head Boy/Head Girl<br><i>(Format 1 · Content 2 · Language 1)</i>"),
    N("Design a poster in not more than 50 words to promote a 'Silent Reading Week' in your school. You are the Secretary of the Literary Club.", "<b>SILENT READING WEEK</b><br><b>Open a Book, Open a World!</b><br>Date: 16–20 November 2026 · Time: Last period daily<br>Venue: School Library and Classrooms<br>Carry a book of your choice. Phones away!<br>Prizes for the best book review.<br>— Literary Club<br><i>(Format 1 · Content 2 · Language 1)</i>")),
 OR(L("You are Ravi/Ravina. Write a letter to the Editor of a newspaper, in about 120 words, expressing concern about the increasing use of plastic bags in your city and suggesting remedies.", "12, Lal Kothi<br>Jaipur<br>2 November 2026<br>The Editor<br>The Daily Chronicle<br>Jaipur<br>Subject: Menace of plastic bags<br>Sir/Madam,<br>Through your newspaper I wish to draw attention to the growing use of plastic bags in our city. They choke drains, harm stray animals and spoil our parks. Shopkeepers hand them out freely and customers seldom object. I request the authorities to enforce the ban strictly and fine offenders. Citizens should carry cloth bags, and shops may offer paper bags at a small price. Schools can also run awareness drives. If we act together, our city can be clean again.<br>Yours faithfully<br>Ravi/Ravina" + FL),
    L("You are Anil/Anita, Secretary of the Science Club. Write a formal email in about 120 words to the Principal, requesting permission to organise a one-day visit to the Jawahar Science Centre for Classes 9 and 10.", "<b>To:</b> principal@mastermindschool.example<br><b>From:</b> sciencesecretary@mastermindschool.example<br><b>Subject:</b> Request for permission – visit to Jawahar Science Centre<br>Respected Madam/Sir,<br>The Science Club wishes to organise an educational visit to the Jawahar Science Centre on Saturday, 21 November 2026, for the students of Classes 9 and 10. The centre has working models, a planetarium and a live demonstration hall that will help students link textbook lessons with practical ideas. We shall leave at 8 a.m. in school buses accompanied by two teachers and return by 4 p.m. The cost, about ₹250 per student, will be shared by the participants. I request you kindly to grant permission.<br>Yours obediently<br>Anil/Anita<br>Secretary, Science Club" + FL)),
 OR(A("As Head Boy/Head Girl, write a speech in about 120–150 words to be delivered in the school assembly on 'Say No to Plastic'.", "<b>Say No to Plastic</b><br>Good morning respected Principal, teachers and my dear friends. Today I wish to speak about a small thing that has become a big problem: plastic. Every day each of us uses a bag, a bottle or a wrapper that will remain on earth for hundreds of years. It blocks drains, harms animals and pollutes our soil and water.<br>We cannot clean the world in a day, but we can begin with ourselves. Let us carry cloth bags, use steel bottles and refuse plastic cutlery. Let us persuade our families to do the same. Remember, a river is saved by every drop that is not polluted. If each of us changes a single habit, our school will become plastic-free by December. Thank you." + FA),
    A("You are a student of Class 9. Write an article for the school magazine in about 120–150 words on 'Why Reading Still Matters'.", "<b>Why Reading Still Matters</b><br>by Rahul/Rashmi, Class 9<br>In an age of videos and games, many young people ask why they should read at all. The answer is simple: reading is the only activity that makes us think while we enjoy. A video shows us a picture; a book makes us paint our own.<br>Reading improves vocabulary, widens knowledge and strengthens concentration. It also teaches empathy, for while reading a story we live in another person's shoes. Students who read regularly write better and speak with confidence.<br>The habit can begin with ten minutes a day. Choose a book you like, find a quiet corner and switch off the phone. Soon the pages will become friends. As someone has said, a reader lives a thousand lives before dying. Why not begin today?" + FA)),
 OR(E("Write a narrative essay in 150–180 words on 'A Day I Will Never Forget'.", "It was the morning of my first inter-school debate, and my hands were as cold as ice. I had prepared for two weeks, yet when I stood on the stage and looked at the rows of faces, every word vanished from my mind.<br>For a moment there was silence. Then I remembered my teacher's advice: 'Take a breath and speak to one friendly face.' I found my friend Meera in the third row, and she smiled. I took a deep breath and began with a simple sentence. Slowly, the lines returned, and my voice grew steady. When I finished, the hall rang with applause.<br>I did not win the first prize; I stood second. But that day I learnt that fear shrinks when we face it. Even now, whenever I am nervous, I recall that moment on the stage, and the memory gives me courage." + FE),
    E("Write a story in 150–180 words that begins: 'The lights went out suddenly, and the whole building was silent.'", "The lights went out suddenly, and the whole building was silent. Sanjay, who was alone in the library finishing his project, froze. Outside the window the storm roared. He took out his phone, but the battery was dead.<br>He felt his way along the shelves, remembering the way to the door. Halfway there he heard a soft sound behind him. His heart thumped. A tiny meow followed, and a small kitten jumped on his feet. Sanjay laughed in relief and picked her up.<br>With the kitten in his arms, he reached the corridor, where the caretaker, Ramu Kaka, was coming with a lantern. 'Thank God you are safe,' said the old man. Sanjay told him about the kitten, and together they gave her warm milk in the staff room.<br>The next morning the kitten was adopted by the class and named 'Torch'. Moral: courage grows when we think calmly in the dark." + FE)),
], G=[
 P("""<p>Last Sunday, our class (a) ______ a picnic to the Sisodia Rani Garden. We left at seven in the morning, and by the time the bus reached the garden, the sun (b) ______ . All of us (c) ______ our lunch under a large tree. If it (d) ______ tomorrow, we shall not go for another trip.</p>""",
   [m("(a)", ["went on", "goes on", "going on", "had gone on"]), m("(b)", ["had risen", "rise", "has risen", "rising"]), m("(c)", ["enjoyed", "enjoy", "enjoys", "enjoying"]), m("(d)", ["rains", "will rain", "rained", "rain"])], title="Complete the paragraph by choosing the correct options for blanks (a)–(d)."),
 g("Rearrange the words to make a meaningful sentence: the / library / books / many / has / our / school.", "Our school library has many books."),
 g("Rearrange: is / the / of / source / main / river / water / this / for / the / town.", "This river is the main source of water for the town."),
 g("Rearrange: had / left / reached / the / train / station / we / when / the.", "The train had left when we reached the station."),
 g("Report the statement: Ravi said to his mother, \"I will help you in the kitchen.\"", "Ravi told his mother that he would help her in the kitchen."),
 g("Join using a relative pronoun: The girl won the prize. She sits next to me.", "The girl who sits next to me won the prize."),
 g("Rewrite as a Type 1 conditional: Work hard. You will pass.", "If you work hard, you will pass."),
])

